  "id": "expedition-base-set-booster-box",
  "name": "Expedition Base Set booster box",
  "category": "product_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "Sealed Expedition Base Set booster boxes, sold from 15 September 2002, each came with one oversized box topper lying on top of the packs, a jumbo copy of Alakazam, Feraligatr, Tyranitar or Venusaur. They are 1/12 to 4/12, the first of the twelve box toppers Wizards of the Coast gave its e-Card series, and PSA grades them as a set of their own, Expedition Box Topper. Since they slid around loose on top of the packs, many have small dings.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Oversized promos of the e-Card series",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/10-oversized-promos-e-card-series/30387"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: the e-Card box toppers and the clear plastic Skyridge cards",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/does-anyone-remember-the-clear-plastic-cards/10584"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: List of all English sets recognized by PSA",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/list-of-all-english-sets-recognized-by-psa/30868"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Box Topper (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 27 July 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260727023621/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Box_Topper_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
